SEQUENCE:0
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260910T111500
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260910T123000
SUMMARY:Experimental/Behavioural – Lionel Page (UQ) – Momentum through 
 Strategic Complementarity
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Lionel Page: “Momentum through Strategic Complementarity”\n
 https://sites.google.com/site/liopage/home\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.u
 s/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAGG.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle 
 Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nWhy does suc
 cess sometimes breed success in dynamic competition? Existing work on mome
 ntum has largely focused on mechanisms operating through individual behavi
 our\, such as changing incentives\, beliefs\, or psychological responses t
 o winning and losing. We study a different channel arising from strategic 
 interaction within teams. In a weakest-link team contest\, individual effo
 rts are strategic complements: the return to exerting high effort depends 
 on the expected contribution of one's teammate. Competitive outcomes can t
 herefore affect subsequent behaviour because they provide information abou
 t a persistent strategic partner. In that setting\, we find that a (random
 ) win substantially increases subsequent effort relative to a (random) los
 s. The effect operates largely through losers reducing effort and translat
 es into higher team minimum effort. The results suggest that competitive o
 utcomes can generate momentum through rational inference combined with str
 ategic complementarity. Outcomes provide information about the likely cont
 ribution of a persistent teammate\; this information changes the return to
  one's own effort and thereby propagates into subsequent collective perfor
 mance.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAG
 G.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
