SUMMARY:Macroeconomics – Sephorah Mangin (ANU) – Competitive Dispersion
 \, Price Dispersion\, and Markups
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Sephorah Mangin: “Competitive Dispersion\, Price Dispersion\,
  and Markups”\nhttp://www.sephorahmangin.info/index.htm\n\nZoom: https:/
 /unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vCa.1&from=a
 ddon\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT
 :\nHow does the distribution of competition across buyers affect markups a
 nd price dispersion? To answer this question\, we introduce the concept of
  competitive dispersion. Competitive dispersion refers to dispersion in th
 e degree of effective competition for different buyers. We study the effec
 ts of competitive dispersion on markups and price dispersion in a Burdett-
 Judd search-theoretic model of imperfect competition. We show that greater
  competitive dispersion can either increase or decrease both the aggregate
  markup and price dispersion.\n We calibrate the model and find that a 10%
  increase in competitive dispersion relative to the efficient benchmark le
 ads to a 2.58% increase in the aggregate markup\, a 3.84\\% increase in pr
 ice dispersion\, and a 2.02% decrease in welfare.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vC
 a.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
