SUMMARY:Macroeconomics – Lukasz Rachel (UCL) – Brothers in Arms: Moneta
 ry-Fiscal Interactions Without Ricardian Equivalence
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Lukasz Rachel: “Brothers in Arms: Monetary-Fiscal Interaction
 s Without Ricardian Equivalence”\nhttps://sites.google.com/site/lukaszra
 chel/\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThC
 Ysc9fs2jh2vCa.1&from=addon\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJK
 urX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nBrothers in Arms: We derive analytical determinac
 y conditions and closed-form equilibrium dynamics when government debt is 
 households' net wealth. We show that the Taylor principle is neither neces
 sary nor sufficient for local determinacy: the active/passive distinction 
 is replaced by a single boundary in the monetary-fiscal policy space. Tran
 sitory shocks — fiscal\, monetary\, and cost-push — have persistent ef
 fects transmitted over time through debt dynamics. Debt persistence is its
 elf shaped by the policy rules. This has fundamental consequences for how 
 policy determines the inflationary impact of shocks. It also underscores t
 he critical role of debt maturity in driving the equilibrium dynamics.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/84055677057?pwd=q1KyfcUkOWfMfEThCYsc9fs2jh2vC
 a.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
