SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Jinjing Chen (University of Melbourne) 
 – Air Pollution and Road Safety: The Role of Agricultural Burning in Pak
 istan
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3057
DESCRIPTION:Jinjing Chen: “Air Pollution and Road Safety: The Role of Agr
 icultural Burning in Pakistan”\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/813472
 71549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.ap
 p.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nRoad traffic accidents impose sub
 stantial social costs\, especially in low- and middle-income countries\, y
 et the environmental determinants of accident risk remain poorly understoo
 d. This paper studies the effect of agricultural burning induced air pollu
 tion on road accidents in Punjab\, Pakistan\, from 2022 to 2025\, using ad
 ministrative emergency accident records. I combine VIIRS active-fire detec
 tions with HYSPLIT-simulated smoke plume trajectories to predict whether s
 moke from fires outside a local area is transported into it\, and use this
  predicted smoke exposure as an instrument for local air pollution exposur
 e. This approach allows me to estimate the causal effect of agricultural-b
 urning-induced air pollution on road accidents. I then examine the mechani
 sms underlying this effect by disentangling two channels: an air-pollution
  channel\, through which pollution may impair cognitive performance and dr
 iving behavior\, and a visibility channel\, through which smoke reduces si
 ght distance and worsens driving conditions. Finally\, I quantify the cont
 ribution of transboundary smoke from Indian Punjab and identify the upwind
  burn locations that generate the largest downstream road-safety externali
 ties\, with implications for spatially targeted enforcement.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bf5bb10d1f05b0ebe605436ec0dac9f2@generated
DTSTAMP:20260905T203919Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260905T203919Z
