DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260904T141000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Melbourne:20260904T145000
SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Kaiyue Chen (University of Melbourne) –
  Public EV Charging Stations in the Workplace
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3058
DESCRIPTION:Kaiyue Chen: “Public EV Charging Stations in the Workplace”
 \n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65k
 UhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nAB
 STRACT:\nMidday electricity is increasingly cheap and clean\, making workp
 lace EV charging an attractive way to shift charging toward hours of abund
 ant renewable generation. But as electricity becomes cheaper\, scarcity sh
 ifts from energy to access to charging bays. Existing per-kWh prices do li
 ttle to allocate this scarce capacity: chargers are often allocated on a f
 irst-come\, first-served basis\, and drivers may continue occupying bays a
 fter charging is complete. We develop a model of parking pricing in which 
 drivers differ in their willingness to pay for charging and their costs of
  moving vehicles\, and study how parking prices affect whether drivers cha
 rge\, how long they occupy a charger\, and ultimately allocative efficienc
 y. We will later extend the model to endogenize arrival decisions and cong
 estion\, characterize the resulting equilibrium\, and use simulations to c
 ompare alternative policies in terms of social welfare.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
