SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Ellie Peppa (University of Melbourne) –
  Same-Sex Parenting\, Child Outcomes\, and the Role of Stigma
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3060
DESCRIPTION:Ellie Peppa: “Same-Sex Parenting\, Child Outcomes\, and the R
 ole of Stigma”\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJ
 kLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJK
 urX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nA growing body of evidence suggests children rais
 ed by same-sex parents fare comparably to those growing up by different-se
 x parents when it comes to educational outcomes. However\, important gaps 
 remain: existing studies have examined outcome measures within a single st
 age of life among children of female same-sex couples\, and rarely test wh
 ether the well-documented "no-difference" pattern depends on the social co
 ntext families live in. This paper addresses these gaps by studying same-s
 ex versus different-sex parented families at two distinct points in the li
 fe course using whole-of-population administrative data from Australia. Fi
 rst\, we examine psychological\, cognitive and health outcomes in early ch
 ildhood. Second\, we examine early labour market and health outcomes among
  adults who grew up in same-sex parented families. Third\, we test whether
  outcomes at both stages vary systematically by area level stigma towards 
 sexual minorities (proxied by opposition to marriage equality). As we have
  only recently gained access to the data required for this project\, this 
 talk focuses on our motivation and proposed identification strategy rather
  than on results.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
